[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2987399251","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107703#issuecomment-2987399251","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107703","id":2987399251,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yEBhT","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-19T09:28:35Z","updated_at":"2025-06-19T09:31:40Z","body":"I'd say that the cases where the callback is also manually called shouldn't be replaced, they represent cases where it might be important to be able to add functionality in those calls and this change makes refactoring a lot harder\r\n\r\nThis should also be checked for performance ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2987399251/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2987422487","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107703#issuecomment-2987422487","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107703","id":2987422487,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yEHMX","user":{"login":"lodetrick","id":146759331,"node_id":"U_kgDOCL9eow","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146759331?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick","html_url":"https://github.com/lodetrick","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-19T09:35:34Z","updated_at":"2025-06-19T09:43:07Z","body":"I can change those cases, that makes sense.\r\n\r\nFor performance, in theory it should increase performance at the cost of more memory. I used the `callable_mp` code as a starting point.\r\nSince when it is called, the current method would pack the args into a `Variant **`, then unpack it when calling the in-between method, which would again pack into `Variant **`, calling `emit_signalp`. This is opposed to the proposed method which only packs the one time before calling `emit_signalp`\r\n\r\nAs for memory, the only difference in memory is that the new callable uses:\r\n```\r\nstruct Data {\r\n    Object *instance;\r\n    uint64_t object_id;\r\n    StringName signal_name;\r\n} data;\r\n```\r\nWhile the current callable uses:\r\n```\r\nstruct Data {\r\n    T *instance;\r\n    uint64_t object_id;\r\n    R (T::*method)(P...);\r\n} data;\r\n```\r\n\r\nI can look into making `signal_name` a reference, which should lead to no change in memory cost (presuming a reference is the same size as a method pointer).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2987422487/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2988004053","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107703#issuecomment-2988004053","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107703","id":2988004053,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yGVLV","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-19T12:51:00Z","updated_at":"2025-06-19T12:51:24Z","body":"Thanks!\r\n\r\nHowever, personally, I don't find this easier to read. The additional `.bind()` and `.unbind()` calls don't make it immediately clear what it's receiving or re-emitting. You have to find the signal definition of both to understand what's happening.\r\n\r\nOf course, without `callable_sp()` (using only `callable_mp()` and a forwarding method), the original author of the code has to have looked up those signal definitions. But for everyone else reading the code later, you can just look at the forwarding method and see what arguments it receives and passes to `emit_signal()`, in order to quickly get an understanding of what's going on.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2988004053/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2989372069","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107703#issuecomment-2989372069","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107703","id":2989372069,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yLjKl","user":{"login":"lodetrick","id":146759331,"node_id":"U_kgDOCL9eow","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146759331?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick","html_url":"https://github.com/lodetrick","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-19T23:22:10Z","updated_at":"2025-06-19T23:24:30Z","body":"Thanks for the feedback. I see what you mean with `.bind()` being confusing. That being said, I do think that the use of `.unbind()` is more readable as it is just removing the last arguments from the previous signal. The `bind` and `unbind` calls are a minority of cases that can be removed if necessary.\r\n\r\nI'm primarily interested in the cases where the engine essentially just forwards one signal to another, without any change in arguments. That's where I believe that this change has the ability to improve readability and remove boilerplate. Take `TabContainer` for example, it just forwards signals from the internal `TabBar` to itself.\r\n\r\nAs for reading the code later, you should just be able to look at the `ADD_SIGNAL` definition of the outgoing signal and it should be more clear, especially in the cases of signal forwarding.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2989372069/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2993480168","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107703#issuecomment-2993480168","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107703","id":2993480168,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ybOHo","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-21T09:18:16Z","updated_at":"2025-06-21T09:18:16Z","body":"Can't you just use `callable_mp(this, &Object::emit_signal).bind(signal)` instead of adding a new macro?\r\nThough I think that would require having `prebind()` 🤔","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2993480168/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2993646590","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107703#issuecomment-2993646590","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107703","id":2993646590,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yb2v-","user":{"login":"lodetrick","id":146759331,"node_id":"U_kgDOCL9eow","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146759331?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick","html_url":"https://github.com/lodetrick","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-21T15:53:19Z","updated_at":"2025-06-21T15:54:04Z","body":"I thought the exact same thing, which is why I implemented something like `prebind()` on my own branch (https://github.com/lodetrick/godot/tree/bind-map for reference) in an attempt to do this, but in the end it didn't work out because `callable_mp` was unable to take in a `VarArg` method. I tried using `emit_signalp` as an alternative but it was unable to cast `Variant **` to a `Variant`. That method just ended up being a lot more hacky than this method, which is why I went with this.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2993646590/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2993647997","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107703#issuecomment-2993647997","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107703","id":2993647997,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yb3F9","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-21T15:56:47Z","updated_at":"2025-06-21T15:56:47Z","body":"Would it work with `emit_signalv()`? (see e.g. `callv()`, which takes arguments as Array)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2993647997/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2993658615","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107703#issuecomment-2993658615","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107703","id":2993658615,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yb5r3","user":{"login":"lodetrick","id":146759331,"node_id":"U_kgDOCL9eow","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146759331?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick","html_url":"https://github.com/lodetrick","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-21T16:22:16Z","updated_at":"2025-06-21T18:30:16Z","body":"I think that `emit_signalv` might work if there was a new connection flag to use `callv` instead of `callp`, and there was also a `prebind()` method to give the name of the signal. That being said, a typical call might turn into \n\n`connect(\"pressed\", callable_mp(Object::cast_to<Object>(this), &Object::emit_signalv).prebind(\"pressed\"), CONNECT_CALLV)`\n\nThis, in my opinion, is not as readable and makes the code unnecessarily confusing for what should be a simple operation. Note that it needs to cast `this` to an object in order to satisfy how callable_mp stores function pointers. For reference, in this PR, this would be written as:\n\n`connect(\"pressed\", callable_sp(this, \"pressed\"))`\n\nThe `emit_signalv` approach would likely be more expensive due to the `prebind` and extra conversions","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2993658615/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2994256202","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107703#issuecomment-2994256202","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107703","id":2994256202,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yeLlK","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-22T14:46:48Z","updated_at":"2025-06-22T14:46:48Z","body":"> As for reading the code later, you should just be able to look at the `ADD_SIGNAL` definition of the outgoing signal and it should be more clear, especially in the cases of signal forwarding.\r\n\r\nRight, the point I'm trying to make is that, currently, you _don't_ have to look at the `ADD_SIGNAL()` definition in order understand what's going on. Looking at the forwarding method in place makes it clear.\r\n\r\nSo, this change would be a downgrade in readability, in my opinion.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2994256202/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]